  "notes": "The air war's weapons and its objects as targets (docs/air_war/10_WEAPONS.md). What a weapon is (its mass, guidance, submunitions, range, the year it came into service, how it is delivered) is encyclopedic (wiki_weapons, gwaps_vol3 for the 1991 nomenclature, mig27_book for the Soviet delivery methods). What it does is a game value: footprint_m (how near an aim point it must fall) and effect (the chance it puts that aim point out of action, by target class), calibrated against what campaigns achieved (sorties to drop a bridge, guided against unguided hit rates, runway closures: docs/air_war/09_BALANCE.md section 9), never a weapon-effects table. laydown_reliability: an unretarded bomb dropped from low level has no time to arm (the Falklands: 25 bombs on ships, 11 went off, navalgazing_falklands).",
